# Some host terminals never answer the OSC 10/11 default-color queries (observed
# on the OHOS terminal). Panes then keep the VT library's built-in
# white-on-black defaults, so reverse video (SGR 7) resolves to black-on-white
# and becomes invisible on a light terminal — a TUI that highlights its mouse
# selection that way (e.g. codex) looks like it has no selection at all.
# Resolve reverse video against an app-palette fallback in that case, without
# changing the pane's reported default colors (applications infer light/dark
# from those, and a wrong guess re-themes the whole app).
